BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ironman703venicejesolo-w1-s4-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261112T063838Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270204
SUMMARY:◆ Legs
DESCRIPTION:Legs - maintenance. Keep glute-med: cycling+running together 
 is a known ITBS risk and hip abductor weakness is the named driver. LOWE
 R-LEG AND FOOT\, about 5 min at the end: tibialis anterior raises 3 x 15
 -20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel walks 2 x 20 m\, eccentric d
 orsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band\, short-foot holds 3 x 30 s per s
 ide\, tennis ball under the arch 60 s. An 8-week RCT in amateur runners 
 raised lactate threshold velocity 5.9% with intrinsic foot work - but th
 at was 30 min DAILY\, so treat this as maintaining the tissue that faile
 d on 7 Sep\, not as a 5.9% gain.\n\nWeek 1 of 12 - Base\nADMIN FIRST: (1
 ) book the certificato medico agonistico - Italy legally requires an ECG
 -based sports medical on the FITRI form\, and without it you are not iss
 ued a race pack. Schedule by February. (2) Ramp-test FTP on the D100 thi
 s week and rescale the sweet-spot watts below - every bike split is a gu
 ess until you do. (3) RAMADAN starts about Mon 8 Feb and weeks 4-7 are i
 n Abu Dhabi (22 Feb - 20 Mar)\; weeks 2-7 are built around both. Swim go
 es to FOUR short sessions - frequency beats volume\, fatigue compromises
  motor learning. SESSION COUNT: 3 runs\, 3-4 swims\, 2 bikes\, 1 legs\, 
 6 days with Thursday off. That is ~9-10 h/week\, which is INTERMEDIATE v
 olume - MyProCoach's beginner 70.3 plan averages 7 h. If adherence slips
 \, scale to the beginner shape rather than abandoning weeks. CUT ORDER: 
 (1) Monday easy run\, (2) the fourth swim\, (3) Wednesday legs. Never cu
 t the long ride\, the long run\, or below three swims.\n80 days to IRONM
 AN 70.3 Venice-Jesolo.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
