DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:◆ Legs
DESCRIPTION:Legs - maintenance\, 30 min. One session keeps strength throu
 gh the peak weeks. Glute-med and the lower-leg block\, nothing heavy. LO
 WER-LEG AND FOOT\, about 5 min at the end: tibialis anterior raises 3 x 
 15-20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel walks 2 x 20 m\, eccentric
  dorsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band\, short-foot holds 3 x 30 s per
  side\, tennis ball under the arch 60 s. An 8-week RCT in amateur runner
 s raised lactate threshold velocity 5.9% with intrinsic foot work - but 
 that was 30 min DAILY\, so treat this as maintaining the tissue that fai
 led on 7 Sep\, not as a 5.9% gain.\n\nWeek 9 of 12 - Peak\nOPEN WATER ST
 ARTS - the single highest-consequence item in this plan. 90 of 120 sudde
 n deaths in US triathlon occurred in the swim\, and the mechanism is col
 d-water panic\, not fitness. You should already have done 5-6 cold immer
 sions over the winter\; this is where it gets applied in a wetsuit.\n24 
 days to IRONMAN 70.3 Venice-Jesolo.
